part.text:
Fixed in `packages/docusaurus-utils/src/markdownLinks.ts:105` — the Markdown-link detection regex was matching `.md` in the middle of URLs, so `![img](./file.md__static_image_assets__/image.png)` had its `./file.md` part rewritten to a permalink, turning the image URL into an absolute path that then got looked up in `/static`.

The regex now:
- requires the `.md`/`.mdx` extension to be followed by a URL delimiter (`)`, `>`, whitespace, `#`, `?`, or end of line), so paths like `file.md__static_image_assets__/image.png` or `file.md_asset/1.png` are no longer matched;
- skips the `http(s)`/`@site` exclusion after an optional `<`, so `<https://.../file_(1).md>` is no longer detected as a Markdown link (also excluded `<` from the filename characters to prevent backtracking);
- allows stray spaces after `(`, as the existing `handles stray spaces` test snapshot expects.

All 14 `markdownLinks.test.ts` tests pass (including the previously failing `does not replace non-Markdown links` and `handles stray spaces`), and the full `docusaurus-utils` + `docusaurus-mdx-loader` suites pass except a pre-existing, unrelated `globUtils.test.ts` HOME_DIR snapshot failure that also fails at baseline.
